A||||7||ChadMan||Car pics (after Oreif/Old Lar treatment)||||10||
Z||000000||ChadMan||07-24-2000||03:52 PM||||Yesterday I washed my car, then gave it the Oreif/Old Lar recommended finish treatment (Meguiar's body scrub, followed by Meguiar's Deep Crystal polish).  I was too darn tired to do the last step (Deep Crystal wax) but will do so before Thursday.  Thanks, guys - I didn't think my tired paint could look this good again.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88Coupe4.jpg"> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88Coupe5.jpg"> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88Coupe6.jpg"> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88Coupe7.jpg"> <P>See you in Louisville!||||reg||10
Z||000001||fiero56||07-24-2000||03:57 PM||||You're ahaead of me. Looks VERY good! Hope mine turns out well.<P>What do you recommend for removing existing wax so I can redo my finish before nationals?||||reg||1
Z||000002||Old Lar||07-24-2000||04:23 PM||||Meguires Cleaner.  Red bottle with 1 on it.  After you wash the car and have it "clean" you go over it with the #1 step.  A random orbital buffer is real handy to put this stuff on.  The stuff looks like watery wax.  After you rub it in, then you get to buff it off..clean cotten  (lots of fresh cotton rags).  You are removing old wax and bonded dirt.  This is the hardest step getting all the crud off the finish.  If the finish is real bad Meguires has a putty to get the real tough stuff off. (I've never used it).<P>Next step is Meguires polish a red bottle with a 2.  Repeat first step wih this stuff.  It will make the car shine, but offers no protection.<P>Then step 3 Meguires wax. Repeat above steps.<P>Then some good carnuba wax.<P>Meguires has up to 7 (steps) materials to really get the car looking good.<P>Water won't stick to the car when your finished.  However it is so shiny, it makes a great target for the birds.  The shock of that shiny object below makes them lose it. That sticks.<BR><p>[This message has been edited by Old Lar (edited 07-24-2000).]||||reg||14
Z||000003||Gokart||07-24-2000||08:17 PM||||Nice work Chadman! I used the same Maguires 3-step system too before I took the pics I posted yesterday! Had to do a little wet-sanding here and there first then buffed with rubbing compound. Did you get the detailers spray for touch-ups after?<P>------------------<BR> Marc                     87GT||||reg||14
Z||000004||87ECO5||07-24-2000||08:24 PM||||<B>WOW!!!!!</B>  That is <I>NOT</I> the same car I followed to Indy two months ago!    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Beautiful job, Chad!  Can you stop by my place on your way down to Louisville on Thursday and make mine look like that!?    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||14
Z||000005||ChadMan||07-24-2000||09:30 PM||||Thanks, guys.  Scott, I'd be glad to, but your car looks better than this already.<P>Marc, yeah, I've got some Quik Detailer too - it's good stuff for a once-over right after a wash job.  Your car looks great too!<P>Drew, I second Old Lar's recommendation for Meguiar's Body Scrub.  My car's first owner gave it a half-a$$ wash job, then threw a bra on over some bug guts, then drove it like that for two years.  The Body Scrub removed some of those bug guts that had been on the car since 1991!||||reg||1
Z||000006||2M4 Dale||07-25-2000||12:00 AM||||Looks Great Chad !!! I love all that Meguiars stuff. I Turtle waxed my Fiero the day before Mid-Ohio. Since then all I've done is wash and use Meguiars "Quik Wax". I think it looks pretty darn good if I don't say so myself...lol<P>See you in Columbus I think...are you caravaning down with COFE ? If not see you in Louiseville.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Oreif||07-25-2000||02:40 AM||||The car came out Great! I would recommend a once a year coat of the #2 polish and just keep it waxed regularly to keep that great shine. If you have areas that are slightly more faded or scratched and the Body scrub or #1 doesn't work Meguires has a light tan bottle that is called "Fine Cut Cleaner" It is slightly more abrasive than the body scrub. It's half way between rubbing compound and the #1 cleaner. I used it on me Saturn after some dweeb scrapped the back fender.  (Saturn has same plastic as Fiero's)<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg"> ||||reg||1
